            <ArticleTitle>Isolated bilateral ostial coronary artery stenoses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>993-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isolated coronary ostial narrowing is rare and most often attributed to atherosclerotic disease of the aorta. A man with isolated, bilateral stenoses of the coronary ostia is presented, who also had severe peripheral vascular disease. A review of previous reports concerning coronary ostial disease is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
